# ⚓ ANCHOR: Skein.jl
# This is the canonical authority for the Skein.jl repository.

id: "org.hyperpolymath.Skein.jl"
version: "1.2.0"
clade: "fv"        # Julia-vocabulary clade (authoritative in CLADE.a2ml)
status: "active"

# Mission
mission: "A standalone knot-theoretic database library for Julia (ADR-0001, 2026-09-26): store knots as Gauss codes (or canonical planar diagrams via the optional KnotTheory.jl weakdep extension), auto-compute and index invariants (Jones, genus, Seifert circles) on insert, and answer invariant/equivalence queries over an embedded SQLite store. Serves general Julia users first. QuandleDB — which hosts the KRL resolution-language implementation — and Tangle are separate projects that CONSUME this library; consumption defines neither purpose nor architecture (INTEGRATION.adoc). The 'maths analogue of a graph database' is the owner's aspirational framing, not a committed implementation — see the grounding note."

# Grounding (2026-06) — supersedes the earlier graph-DB "realignment"
grounding:
  date: "2026-06-18"
  role: "Skein is an independent Julia library: storage + invariants + equivalence + queries over an embedded SQLite store. QuandleDB is the in-estate application that wraps it (persistence + invariant/equivalence face); KRL is a resolution DSL implemented there — its operations are not Skein components and Skein is not 'the Retrieve leg'. See .machine_readable/6a2/ECOSYSTEM.a2ml and docs/decisions/ADR-0001."
  withdrawn: "An earlier draft proposed a typed knot-relationship (edge) layer + traversal (connected-sum DAG, skein triples L+/L-/L0, mutation/crossing-change; schema v5). That was authored on a MISTAKEN 'KRL = query language' model and is WITHDRAWN. Skein-relation resolution belongs to the KRL surface / Tangle core / QuandleDB Resolve layer, not necessarily Skein's persistence layer. Any edge/traversal or schema change must be re-grounded against the KRL 4-layer architecture first."

# SSG Configuration (Unified boj-server build)
ssg:
  engine: "casket"
  output_dir: "public"
  boj_trigger: true
  cartridge: "ssg-mcp"

# Relationships
parents:
  - "org.hyperpolymath.boj-server"
